# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Measurement data must never be committed.  This repository's history already
# contains real scans (the user decided not to purge it), so these rules plus
# the CI guard in .github/workflows/ci.yml are the whole prevention story.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Raw instrument formats.  Deliberately UNANCHORED: a stray scan copied into
# any directory of the tree is caught, not just one at the repository root.
*.sxm
*.3ds
*.dat
*.ibw
*.spm
*.stp
*.nid
*.sm4

# Measurement data trees at the repository root.  Anchored with a leading
# slash ON PURPOSE: a future tests/data/ fixture directory must not be
# silently swallowed by a bare `data/` rule.
/sample/
/data/
/raw_data/
/measurements/

# Bulk arrays and containers.  Also UNANCHORED, so these deliberately match
# binaries placed under tests/ as well (e.g. tests/data/standard.npy): a binary
# test fixture therefore needs `git add -f`, or a non-ignored format (CSV/text)
# instead.  This strictness is intentional - no negation rules here, so nothing
# can slip a measurement array past the guard.  Note the root-anchored tree
# rules above (/sample/, /data/, ...) are anchored precisely so they do NOT
# over-match a future `tests/data/` directory.
*.npy
*.npz
*.h5
*.hdf5
*.mat
